Accelerated charges, Larmor and reaction limits (@em-accelerated-charge: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @electromagnetism, #source "../sources/Classical-Electromagnetism-Fitzpatrick.lingua#r_7NH7AZZH3NZ2FHJ4K5VBT49F6H", #source "../sources/Electromagnetism-Tong.lingua#r_278NEA0Z85RJZSPXQ8G55E3SR1", #electromagnetism "Antennas-gain-aperture-efficiency-and-reciprocity.lingua#r_1578RDNQH3K3RR4GWDMHGP292K") { r_19J7GRVJRGWX97DXT5S7P5G5MS
**Read:** [Classical Electromagnetism — Richard Fitzpatrick](../sources/Classical-Electromagnetism-Fitzpatrick.lingua#r_7NH7AZZH3NZ2FHJ4K5VBT49F6H), accelerated charges and relativistic radiation; [Electromagnetism — David Tong](../sources/Electromagnetism-Tong.lingua#r_278NEA0Z85RJZSPXQ8G55E3SR1), radiation, energy balance and classical limits.

For a nonrelativistic point charge in vacuum, instantaneous Larmor power is q²a²/(6π ε₀c³). It describes a radiative loss in a classical model with an appropriate smooth trajectory. Derive it from the far acceleration field and angular integration before extending the result to relativistic motion.

Distinguish velocity and acceleration field terms in the Liénard–Wiechert construction and account for retarded direction/time. Relativistic beaming and frequency changes require the actual relativistic formulas; adding a guessed γ factor to the nonrelativistic expression is not a derivation. Compare the energy supplied by an external force with radiated and near-field energy.

Radiation reaction introduces subtle issues including self-energy, reduction of order and the domain of a point-particle approximation. Analyze the limitations of a chosen equation rather than treating runaway or preacceleration solutions as ordinary predictions for all scales. Classical radiation does not explain stable atomic spectra. Connect to quantum/radiation-physics subjects where photon emission and microscopic structure matter, while preserving the classical domain useful for antennas, beams and macroscopic radiation measurements.

**Continue:** [Antennas, gain, aperture, efficiency and reciprocity](Antennas-gain-aperture-efficiency-and-reciprocity.lingua#r_1578RDNQH3K3RR4GWDMHGP292K).

